<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi bourse contributes to debt repayment fund.</title>
<headline>Karachi bourse contributes to debt repayment fund.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's main Karachi Stock Exchange (KSE) and some of its members have contributed 18.5 million rupees to a fund set up by new Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif to help repay foreign debts, the KSE said on Monday.</p>
<p>The KSE has also offered to list profit-bearing schemes on the exchange free of cost to make the scheme more attractive and successful, a KSE statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;This will encourage the general public to contribute generously to these schemes,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
